    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. just to be super clear though, since it's CIF, the seller pays the freight and the insurance, right? but if the ship hits a storm and the cargo gets damaged before it reaches Hamburg, who is the one filing the actual insurance claim? is it the seller or me (the buyer)?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for paying the freight and providing insurance for the goods during transit. However, if the ship encounters a storm and the cargo gets damaged before it reaches Hamburg, the responsibility for filing the insurance claim falls on you, the buyer. This is because the risk of loss transfers to you once the goods are loaded onto the vessel at the port of shipment. So, if the cargo is damaged during transit, you would be the one to file the claim with the insurance company. It's important to ensure that you have adequate insurance coverage for the goods and to keep all necessary documentation, as you will need to provide proof of insurance and evidence of the damage when filing the claim. Remember, in the world of shipping, it's always better to be prepared for the unexpected, especially when dealing with valuable goods.",
